    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, this is inevitable with Lean's formalism / mathlib's definition of <code>Group</code>. <code>Group</code> includes a <em>function</em> <code>inv : G → G</code> and you need AC to extract data out of the <code>Prop</code> <code>∀ x ∈ G, ∃ y ∈ G, y * x = e</code></p>",
        "id": 578383894,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruben Van de Velde",
        "timestamp": 1773146474
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(In lean's formalism, strengthening to \"there exists a unique inverse\" doesn't help either.)</p>",
